    description: "Audit-findings 0013 §'Diagnostic findings' #3 lists grpc_server, grpc_stub, ipc_subscriber, mq_publisher, mq_subscriber, websocket_emitter, websocket_listener, rpc, service as 'registry placeholders with no producers' (PRELIM_RESOLVED at filing). The diagnostic-test literal grep used kwarg-form (kind=\"<value>\") and missed assignment-form producers. grpc.py:657 emits kind = \"grpc_stub\" if pattern.type == \"stub\" else \"grpc_client\" and grpc.py:660 emits kind = \"grpc_server\" — both via assignment, not kwarg. These rows should be reclassified UNRESOLVED in audit-findings 0013, and gRPC server/stub/service/servicer/client kinds should be migrated as part of a follow-on Wave 5 sub-PR (likely combined with the grpc framework_dispatch evidence_type fold already shipped in PR #3572). Also check whether the other 7 'no producer' rows (ipc_subscriber, mq_publisher, mq_subscriber, websocket_emitter, websocket_listener, rpc, service) have similar assignment-form producers that the literal-grep missed. Found while shipping Wave 5 PR #1."  # 1a44
